WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
- I have to ask you about this photo.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.360
So here, I'm gonna put it up for you.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.503
This is awesome.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.050
So, here's the thing I
love about this picture.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.520
My kids and actually,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.110
they gravitate towards
Ursula, not Little Mermaid.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.920
They gravitate towards
Gaston not the Beast.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.600
I don't know what's wrong with them.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.780
But does yours gravitate
towards "The Grinch"

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.110
instead of Santa?

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:26.110
- He just loves kind of the
creepy, like aspect of things.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.360
So he would like "Nightmare
Before Christmas"

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.590
which is, you know, a Christmas movie

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.490
- Yeah.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.230
- But he likes like the creepyness of it.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.063
I mean, he loves Santa.

00:00:36.063 --> 00:00:37.403
He has the sweetest heart.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.150
He, I don't know he is my child.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.870
I like scary movies and
the creepy stuff too.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.870
I swear I have not imposed
any of my stuff onto him.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.130
And this is just what
he likes going for us.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.470
So he loves "The Grinch"

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.780
- It's so funny, 'cause I'm opposite.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.770
Like I don't like anything
scary and my kids love it.

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.507
Like I'm the one sitting
on the couch going,

00:01:01.507 --> 00:01:05.080
"Why can't we just like, watch
like something really happy?"

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.010
Like why does everything
have to scare me here?

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.300
Speaking of children though, Isaiah.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.180
So you sing a duet with him on the record.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.400
And I saw in the special as well

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.560
there's video footage of him as well.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.520
So was he excited to hear
himself on the record?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.930
- He was, I had no idea
what was gonna happen.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.410
He's never been in that
kind of situation before.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.490
I don't think he's even been

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.540
like in the studio with me ever before.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.220
He probably, I don't know
if he knows what I do at all

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.590
but I just thought I could hear his voice

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.410
on it in my head when I was
singing it in the studio.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.460
And I just thought I'd ask him
and see if he might want to.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.120
And he did such a great job
and listening back, like

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.130
I feel like he's just so proud of himself.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.027
And he went to school and he's like,

00:01:46.027 --> 00:01:49.800
"Hey, my songs out, wanna hear my songs."

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.820
And they were like listening
to it in his class.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.190
- I think it's adorable.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.023
And it's cool.

00:01:54.023 --> 00:01:56.140
I think that when we're singers
that our kids take some kind

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.770
of interest in what we
do, that's kind of cool.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.853
Cause we work a lot.

